# Controls what EAS Build uploads in the project archive (monorepo root).
# Found 2026-09-18: with no .easignore, the archive was 3.8 GB — over EAS's
# 2.0 GB upload cap — and every `eas build --platform ios` failed at the
# upload step. The single biggest contributor was apps/mobile/ios/build/
# (2.3 GB of local Xcode DerivedData-style build output from prior local
# builds): it has its own nested apps/mobile/ios/.gitignore entry, but
# eas-cli's archiver doesn't reliably walk nested .gitignore files the way
# `git` itself does, so a deeply-nested ignored directory can still make it
# into the tarball. Listed explicitly here rather than assumed inherited.
#
# This is a monorepo: EAS Build for apps/mobile still needs the workspace
# root (pnpm-workspace.yaml, root package.json, packages/) to resolve
# workspace deps, so this file excludes bulk/irrelevant content rather than
# everything outside apps/mobile.

# Root and per-workspace node_modules — EAS always does a fresh install
# server-side from the lockfile, so shipping any local copy is pure waste.
node_modules/
apps/*/node_modules/
packages/*/node_modules/
services/*/node_modules/

# Xcode/Gradle local build output — regenerated every build, never a build
# input. android/ itself is already fully gitignored (expo-prebuild
# generated, never committed) but excluded explicitly here too for the same
# "don't rely on nested-gitignore support" reason as ios/build/ above.
apps/mobile/ios/build/
apps/mobile/ios/Pods/
apps/mobile/android/

# This session's/agents' local worktree fleet — already gitignored via
# .git/info/exclude (machine-local, so not in the committed .gitignore),
# but that's a git-ignore file, not necessarily one eas-cli's archiver
# reads either. Was ~51 GB at the time this file was added.
.claude/

# Not needed to build the mobile app; large/irrelevant to this archive.
services/
docs/
guideline/
reference/
.git/
apps/web/.next/
apps/web/out/
**/coverage/
*.log
